Time\SpecialChar ~
For\SpecialChar ~
Queue For simplicity we consider 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu =\frac{1}{\left\langle X\right\rangle }.$
\end_inset 

 So 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu =\frac{2}{b}$
\end_inset 

 and thus 
\begin_inset Formula $b=\frac{2}{\mu }$
\end_inset 

.
 So we can write the second moment in terms of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu $
\end_inset 

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\frac{b^{2}}{3}$
\end_inset 

, substituting in 
\begin_inset Formula $b=\frac{2}{\mu }$
\end_inset 

 we have 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\frac{4}{3\mu ^{2}}$
\end_inset 

.
 Substituting in to the P-K formula we recover
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{W}=\frac{2\rho }{3\mu \left(1-\rho \right)}.\]

\end_inset 


\end_deeper 
