\layout Example

Automatic Repeat Request system --- ARQ System.
 
\layout Standard


\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
collapsed false

\layout Standard
\align center 

\begin_inset Include \input{./diagrams/ARQ.eepic}

\end_inset 


\layout Caption

The ARQ System.
\end_inset 

Assume each packet takes 1 millisecond to be transmitted.
\layout Standard

The system waits 
\begin_inset Formula $n-1$
\end_inset 

 milliseconds for an acknowledgement.
 If there is no acknowledgement the system retransmits.
\layout Standard

The probability of an error in a packet is taken to be 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset 

.
 Errors are taken to be independent.
 Assume that packets arrive as a Poisson process with rate 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda $
\end_inset 

.
  Time interval between transmission and re-transmission is 
\begin_inset Formula $1+kn$
\end_inset 

 time units with probability 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(1-p\right)p^{k}$
\end_inset 


\layout Standard

The probability of the service time is
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(X=1+kn\right)=\left(1-p\right)p^{k}\]

\end_inset 

 The expected service time is therefore
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\langle X\right\rangle  & = & \sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\left(1+kn\right)\left(1-p\right)p^{k}\\
 & = & \left(1-p\right)\left(\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }p^{k}+n\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }kp^{k}\right)\\
 & = & 1+\frac{np}{1-p}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 since 
\begin_inset Formula $\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }p^{k}=\frac{1}{1-p}$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }kp^{k}=\frac{p}{\left(1-p\right)^{2}}$
\end_inset 

.
 Thus we can write that
\begin_inset Formula \[
\rho =\frac{\lambda \left(1-p\right)}{1-p+np}\]

\end_inset 

and thus 
\begin_inset Formula \[
1-\rho =\frac{1-\lambda -p\left(n-1-\lambda \right)}{1-p+np}\]

\end_inset 

The second moment of the service time is
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle  & = & \sum _{k=0}^{\infty }\left(1+kn\right)^{2}\left(1-p\right)p^{k}\\
 & = & \left(1-p\right)\left(\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }p^{k}+2n\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }kp^{k}+n^{2}\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }k^{2}p^{k}\right)\\
 & = & 1+\frac{2np}{1-p}+\frac{n^{2}\left(p+p^{2}\right)}{\left(1-p\right)^{2}}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

since 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum _{k=0}^{\infty }k^{2}p^{k}=\frac{p+p^{2}}{\left(1-p\right)^{3}}\]

\end_inset 

 Substitiuting into the P-K formula gives a very ugly formula!
\the_end
